---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';
---
<PageLayout title="About This Site and Its Author" description={`Who runs ${SITE.name}, why the tools were built and how they are kept free, private and useful for exam applicants, students and teachers.`} h1="About this site" crumb="About">
  {/* AUTHOR REVIEW: replace the placeholders below with your real name, photo and background. This page matters a lot for AdSense: real, specific detail builds trust. */}
  <img
    src="/author-placeholder.svg"
    alt="Placeholder portrait of the site author. Replace with a real photo."
    width="160"
    height="160"
    loading="lazy"
    style="border-radius:50%;float:right;margin:0 0 12px 16px;"
  />
  <p>
    Hello, I am <strong>[YOUR NAME]</strong>. I am a teacher, and I built {SITE.name} to solve problems I kept seeing
    around me: students and job applicants stuck on an online form because a photo was 12 KB too large, and teachers
    losing time on jobs that a small program can do in a second.
  </p>
  <h2>My background</h2>
  {/* AUTHOR REVIEW: describe your subject, school or college, years of teaching, and any qualifications. */}
  <p>
    [Add a short paragraph here: the subject you teach, the kind of institution, how many years you have been
    teaching, and what led you to build web tools.]
  </p>
  <h2>What this site offers</h2>
  <p>
    The site has free tools for <a href="/photo-and-signature-resizer/">resizing photos and signatures</a>, working with
    PDFs, calculating percentages, CGPA and age, and running a class. Each tool comes with a written
    <a href="/guides/">guide</a> that explains the idea in plain English with a worked example.
  </p>
  <h2>How the tools work</h2>
  <p>
    Every tool runs inside your browser. When you pick a photo or PDF, it is processed on your own device and is never
    sent to a server. You can read more in the <a href="/privacy-policy/">privacy policy</a>.
  </p>
  <h2>Accuracy and corrections</h2>
  <p>
    I test each tool before publishing it and update guides when something changes. Exam rules differ between
    organisations and change from year to year, so the tools never claim to know the official limits for your exam.
    Always follow the notification for your own form. If you spot a mistake, please tell me through the
    <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
